 The graph of $y = e^x$ is the reflection of the graph of $y = \log x$. Therefore, the graph of $y = f^{-1}(x)$ is the graph that is the reflection of the graph of $y = f(x)$ about the \textbf{y = x} line. 

[asy]
unitsize(0.5 cm);

